{
  "programId": "com.digitalarsenal.flows.cellular-network-ingest",
  "name": "Cellular Network Ingest Flow",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "engineLinkage": "bridge",
  "description": "The INGEST counterpart to cellular-network-aggregate (typed contracts 1.0: FlatBuffers only, no JSON and no base64 between nodes). A cron timer delivers a TimerTick (TICK) to cell-tower-ingest:mark_query, which emits the $FSO FlatSQL query reading the ingest resume marks; hostcap/flatsql-query answers the stored $IRM rows as $FSB chunks to cell-tower-ingest:ingest_plan, which emits ONE ranged HttpRequest (HREQ) for the next chunk. The run travels IN the request: HttpRequest.CONTEXT is a size-prefixed stream of the $APR run contract (ROUTE ingest, PROVIDERS, METHOD, LIMIT, FULL_POPULATION, the per-fetch provider and fetches=1) and the $IRM job the chunk continues (offset, chunk budget, decode context: CSV header row, version-stamped inflate state). hostcap/http-request echoes it on the HttpResponse (HRSP). The chunk is bounded by the Go host's 4 MiB response-body cap, so a 40M-row bulk export is fetched as a sequence of ranged chunks instead of one truncated GET. cell-tower-source's parse and deconflict are REUSED UNCHANGED - parse decodes the body into single-source $TBS reports (and, for a gzip export, the next $IRM decoder resume), deconflict merges them into the $TBS record stream - and cell-tower-ingest:ingest_meta authors the IngestRequest (INGQ: TBS.fbs, source tags, reconcile None because each batch is one CHUNK of the provider's set, provenance) and the candidate next $IRM from the HttpResponse (Content-Range total, row-boundary correction, the header row at chunk 0, the decoder's own next byte when one ran). hostcap/storage-ingest persists the batch through storage.ingest_with_source and answers an IngestResult (INGR). cell-tower-ingest:publish_request advances the mark FROM THE STORAGE RESULT - never at dispatch, so a crash between fetch and store re-fetches one chunk instead of skipping rows invisibly; inserted=0 for a chunk that carried records, or a REFUSED batch, stops the run without a mark - and emits the $IRM to hostcap/storage-write (storage.write, storage_write grant) and to egress, plus the dataset-publication POST (its body an IngestResult) only when a publish URL is configured. HTTP 304 NOT MODIFIED: the host presents the validators it recorded, an unchanged export answers 304 with no body, parse and deconflict pass an empty stream and ingest_meta emits one FlowNotice (FNTC Unchanged) to egress and nothing on meta/records, so nothing is stored or announced and the mark stays put. The flow's runtimeTargets are wasmedge: storage_write is browser-incompatible and this is a timer-driven server ingest lane by construction. The host owns no schedule, no provider list, no chunking policy and no record semantics: it contributes timers, HTTP egress, guarded persistence and the FlatSQL rows that hold the mark.",
